  "presentation_summary": [
    "32-year-old man with severe alcohol dependence and multiple hospitalizations/relapses stopped regular heavy drinking.",
    "Within a day of stopping alcohol he developed generalized tremulousness, nausea, excessive sweating, and two generalized tonic-clonic seizures, prompting hospitalization at a peripheral center.",
    "At 0800 h on day 1 he was disoriented to time, place, and person, tachycardic to 120/min, hypertensive to 150/100 mmHg, tremulous, profusely sweating, restless, uncooperative, and agitated.",
    "Labs showed hypokalemia and hypomagnesemia; noncontrast CT head was normal. CIWA-Ar score was 29, and symptoms had minimal control after 8 mg lorazepam over 1 hour.",
    "Despite high-dose benzodiazepines, CIWA-Ar remained elevated and RASS remained agitated until midazolam and dexmedetomidine were used."
  ],
